  "narrative": {
    "text": "A screenshot of the WHO Digital Health Atlas web application, showing a map of parts of East Africa (South Sudan, Ethiopia, Somalia, Uganda, Kenya, Democratic Republic of the Congo, Burundi) with numbered blue pin markers indicating counts of cataloged digital health implementations at each location (values visible include 2, 4, 6, 30, 34 and 83). A side panel lists implementations for Rwanda, including 'E-Heza Data Solutions', 'Rwanda Health Analytics Platform (RHAP)', 'Rwanda HMIS' and 'DHIS2 for COVID-19 Surveillance', with a toggle to switch the map between 'Sub-national' and 'National' views.",
